From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 21:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethercat: K3 stmmac: update xsk_buff_get_metadata() to
 the 3-arg API

6.18.52 gave the AF_XDP metadata helper an options argument, so it can
tell whether the descriptor actually asked for TX metadata:

  static inline struct xsk_tx_metadata *
  xsk_buff_get_metadata(struct xsk_buff_pool *pool, u64 addr, u32 options);

drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c in the same tree was
updated to match, but the out-of-tree EtherCAT fork still calls the
2-arg form, so the kernel fails to build:

  drivers/net/ethercat/device/K3/stmmac_main-ethercat.c:2595:24: error:
    too few arguments to function 'xsk_buff_get_metadata'

Pass xdp_desc.options, exactly as mainline stmmac_main.c does. The
descriptor is already in scope in stmmac_xdp_xmit_zc().

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethercat/device/K3/stmmac_main-ethercat.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethercat/device/K3/stmmac_main-ethercat.c b/drivers/net/ethercat/device/K3/stmmac_main-ethercat.c
index 93d91ec..7a15a00 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethercat/device/K3/stmmac_main-ethercat.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethercat/device/K3/stmmac_main-ethercat.c
@@ -2592,7 +2592,8 @@ static bool stmmac_xdp_xmit_zc(struct stmmac_priv *priv, u32 queue, u32 budget)
 			tx_desc = tx_q->dma_tx + entry;
 
 		dma_addr = xsk_buff_raw_get_dma(pool, xdp_desc.addr);
-		meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, xdp_desc.addr);
+		meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, xdp_desc.addr,
+					     xdp_desc.options);
 		xsk_buff_raw_dma_sync_for_device(pool, dma_addr, xdp_desc.len);
 
 		tx_q->tx_skbuff_dma[entry].buf_type = STMMAC_TXBUF_T_XSK_TX;
--
Armbian
